course: dictionary
lesson: 6429
title: Myopia and short sight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Myopia is another word for short-sightedness. If you have it, things close to you look clear, but things far away look blurry. «Short sight, or myopia, means far things look blurry and near things clear.» The sentence tells you straight away that short sight and myopia mean the same thing.
explain: Why does this happen? The eye focuses light in front of the retina instead of on it. Glasses or contact lenses with concave (curved-in) lenses help the eye focus properly, so far things look clear again.
explain: The word can also be used in a formal way. «Political myopia» means a lack of foresight: people only think about now and do not think about what will happen later. Look for clue words. Near and far point to eyes, while now and later point to the future.
fact: Myopia means short-sightedness.
fact: With myopia, near things look clear and far things look blurry.
fact: In myopia, the eye focuses light in front of the retina, not on it.
fact: Concave (curved-in) lenses help people with myopia see far things clearly.
fact: In a formal sense, myopia means not thinking about what will happen later, as in «political myopia».
exercise: «Short sight, or myopia, means far things look blurry and near things clear.» What does myopia mean? | A type of camera lens | *Short-sightedness | Long-sightedness | Seeing colours very clearly
exercise: Maya can read her book clearly, but she cannot read the bus number across the road. What might she have? | A toothache | A cold | *Myopia
exercise: «Political myopia» suggests what kind of thinking? | Bright, colourful ideas | Strong eyesight at a great distance | *A lack of thought about what will happen later | Very careful planning for the future
test: Which kind of lens helps a person with myopia see far things clearly? | Flat glass | *Concave (curved-in) lenses | Mirrors
test: In myopia, where does the eye focus light? | On the eyelid | Inside the ear | Behind the lens of the camera | *In front of the retina
exam: Which description best fits myopia? | Eyes that cannot blink | Everything looks bright and coloured | Far things clear and near things blurry | *Near things clear and far things blurry
